== Implementation (2026-11-07) ==
backend/app/cpic_engine.py select_annotation: when no usable row matches the called phenotypes it now returns no
row, with the warning "No CPIC row for <drug> matches the called phenotypes, so none is shown: a row written for a
different result could give the opposite advice. Reported as Unknown." evaluate()'s existing `annotation is None`
branch then reports Unknown with its existing reason. The old line `candidates = matched or usable` and its warning
("showing the strongest available row") are gone. The docstring's step 2 said "the strongest classification (most
cautious)"; that conflation of evidence strength with caution is the misconception the fallback rested on, and it now
says strength measures evidence, not caution. Nothing else in the engine changed: the population choice among rows
that do match, _annotation_matches_calls, evaluate, derive_label and the label mapping are untouched.
The two build-time scripts are not edited: they call the same selector, so they stop grounding on a borrowed row
because it no longer returns one.

== Tests (backend/tests/test_no_borrowed_row.py, 5 passed) ==
Control  the untouched cyp2c19_pm fixture is Ineffective with "Avoid clopidogrel", so the exemplar starts from the
         case it claims to.
AC1      that fixture with clopidogrel's guideline holding only CPIC's Normal Metabolizer row: Unknown; the action is
         evaluate()'s no-match reason and does not contain "use at standard dose"; the no-match warning is present.
AC2      all 16 fixtures, each drug's guideline given every real CPIC row except those matching the called phenotypes:
         every case that reaches the no-match branch is Unknown, and no borrowed row's text reaches its action. The
         positive control requires the warning in each counted case and at least 63 cases, the number measured before
         the fix, so the test cannot pass by never reaching the branch.
AC3      for dpyd_compound_het, pregenerate_explanations.find_annotation and enumerate_cases.cpic_text_for no longer
         return the DPYD activity score 2.0 row for fluorouracil or capecitabine at phenotype Unknown; the runtime is
         asserted Unknown for the same report.
The CPIC wording comes from test-data/reference/cpic_expectations.json; none of it is invented.

